  "verbalization": "n-Octyl sulfate appears to interact with FaDu through a series of molecular pathways involving the CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase enzyme. This enzyme is both a target of n-Octyl sulfate and a target of other compounds, such as 2-Methylheptyl propanoate and a complex organic molecule. The presence of multiple targets suggests a potential mechanism where n-Octyl sulfate may influence the activity of this enzyme, which in turn affects the function of FaDu. The integration of these pathways implies that n-Octyl sulfate could modulate the biological activity of FaDu through the regulation of sialyltransferase activity, potentially altering cellular processes that are critical for the function of FaDu. The evidence supports a role for n-Octyl sulfate in influencing the biological function of FaDu via a mechanism involving the sialyltransferase enzyme, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
